<p id="mwJA"><b id="mwJQ">Transmembrane protease, serine 6</b> (also known as matriptase-2) is an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Enzyme" title="Enzyme" id="mwJg">enzyme</a> that in humans is encoded by the <i id="mwJw">TMPRSS6</i> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Gene" title="Gene" id="mwKA">gene</a>.<sup about="#mwt25" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-entrez_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"entrez"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-entrez-5"}}'><a href="./TMPRSS6#cite_note-entrez-5" id="mwKQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKw">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwLQ">Based on twin studies, mutations in TMPRSS6 gene have a correlation with iron deficiency predisposition.<sup about="#mwt26" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="./TMPRSS6#cite_note-6" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwMg">The protein encoded by this gene is a type II transmembrane serine proteinase that is found attached to the cell surface. The encoded protein may be involved in matrix remodeling processes in the liver.<sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-entrez_5-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"entrez"}}'><a href="./TMPRSS6#cite_note-entrez-5" id="mwMw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNQ">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

